<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyoto</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyoto is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> that served as the imperial capital for over a thousand years. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> the emperor and court remained in Kyoto, while real political power lay with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> in Edo. The shogunate supervised the court closely, and the city remained a major cultural and craft centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyoto.jpg" alt="Kyoto" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nina R from Africa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kyoto,_Japan_(49667780482).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
